{
  "name": "vector_light_pawn_shadows",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "27 phase 4: a pawn throws a shadow away from the lamp that lights it. ROOFED ON PURPOSE \u2014 vanilla's Graphic_Shadow bails on any roofed cell because sunlight does not get in, so inside this room vanilla draws no pawn shadow at all and every shadow in the frame is ours. Two colonists: one four cells from the torch with clear line of sight, one behind a five-cell stub the torch cannot see past. The second must cast NOTHING, which is the property only the mask can supply \u2014 its coverage grid is what answers 'can this lamp see that cell', and vanilla's own glow grid would answer yes because its light bends around corners. Three arms: vanilla, mask + beam without pawn shadows, and with them, so the shadows can be told apart from the light that motivates them. The lit pawn stands TWO cells from the torch, not four: a shadow needs lit ground to fall on, and at four cells the floor is already near black, so the shadow was geometrically correct and invisible \u2014 a 9% darkening of near-black rounds to nothing.",
